QuestGuidance.Register("en",352,{
[11233]="70000D11\n1\tCollect Edilina Proudfoot's pie\tHolly Hornblower's home is north of the Hobbiton main square. Edilina Proudfoot has one of Holly's bad pies, which you should take back to her as quickly as possible. Make sure no hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, as Holly doesn't want to be bothered with them asking for a slice, especially since she has to bake fresh pies for all her customers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[11234]="70000D12\n1\tCollect Daisy Hornblower's pie\tHolly Hornblower's home is north of the Hobbiton main square. Daisy Hornblower has one of Holly's bad pies, which you should take back to her as quickly as possible. Make sure no hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, as Holly doesn't want to be bothered with them asking for a slice, especially since she has to bake fresh pies for all her customers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[11235]="70000D03\n1\tCollect Opal Goodbody's pie\tHolly Hornblower's home is north of the Hobbiton main square. Opal Goodbody has one of Holly's bad pies, which you should take back to her as quickly as possible. Make sure no hungry hobbits catch a whiff of the pie, as Holly doesn't want to be bothered with them asking for a slice, especially since she has to bake fresh pies for all her customers. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[11236]="7000187A\n1\tDefeat Dead-aim Ongbúrz in Gurzlum (total: 5)\030Defeat Grim Ongbúrz in Gurzlum (total: 5)\tThe Orc-camp Gurzlum is south-west of Gatson's fields. Farmer Gatson is sure the Orcs will attack his farm again if they are not deterred first.\n2\tTalk to Gatson\tGatson is back at his farm, north-east of the Orc-camp. You should tell Gatson of your success in thinning the Orc threat at Gurzlum.\n",
[11237]="70015E2C\n1\tDestroy worm-eggs (total: 12)\030Defeat Fotkûrz, Worm-master\tWorm-eggs can be found in nests throughout the ruins of Pembar, north-east of Echad Eregion. Lengliel has asked you to destroy as many of the worm-eggs at Pembar as you are able. Fortkûrz the Worm-master may be found wandering in Pembar.\n2\tTalk to Lengliel at Echad Eregion\tLengliel is at Echad Eregion, south-west of Pembar. You should return to Lengliel and let her know that you have destroyed many worm-eggs and have defeated Fotkûrz the Worm-master, as she bade you.\n",
[11238]="7005B001\n1\tCollect dwarf-helmets (total: 4)\030Collect dwarf-shields (total: 8)\030Collect dwarf-swords (total: 10)\tFallen dwarves can be found at Durin's Stone. You should collect arms and armour from fallen dwarves at Azanulbizar.\n2\tDeliver the dwarf-helmets, dwarf-shields, and dwarf-swords to Thorin at Amdân\tThorin can be found at Amdân. You have collected a great deal of arms and armour from the fallen. You should deliver them to Thorin at Amdân.\n",
[11239]="7005339B\n1\tStolen treasures can be found in the warrens of Tûn Melen. Tautila told you Sharkey's Men have been stealing and collecting odd objects to impress Sharkey. He has asked you to recover the stolen 'treasures'.\t\n2\tDeliver the 'treasures' to Tautila in the warrens of Tûn Melen\tTautila can be found in the warrens of Tûn Melen. You have recovered a strange collection of items stolen by Sharkey's Men in the Gladden Fields. You should return to Tautila.\n",
[11240]="700717A1\n1\tGather blighted mushrooms (total: 5)\tTálbiral is in need of new mushrooms to study and asked you to gather some for him. He mentioned the ones he needs can be found just outside of Laivárth.\n2\tReturn the blighted mushrooms to Tálbiral\tYou have gathered the mushrooms that Tálbiral requested. Return to him in Laivárth so that he can begin his studies.\n",
[11241]="7006AE12\n1\tTalk to Hanâth at The Din of Arms\tFind and speak with Hanâth at The Din of Arms in the Tor Gardens. Shemâya, a wine-merchant of Umbar Baharbêl has come to Dâr Laja to file a complaint against a frequent visitor to the shop. She suggests first meeting with his wife, Hanâth at The Din of Arms in the Tor Gardens.\n2\tSearch for Hanâth's husband in Tâkhdar\tHanâth's husband is somewhere in Tâkhdar, likely in Kheb Hanût. A frantic woman is looking for her husband, who has gotten himself banned from every wine-house for drunken behaviour. She suspects he is still drinking somewhere in Tâkhdar.\n3\tSearch for a drunken man in Kheb Hanût\tHanâth's husband is probably in Tâkhdar in the black market at Kheb Hanût. Search for someone who seems particularly inebriated in the cellars.\n4\tSpeak with Hanâth's inebriated spouse\tHanâth's husband is drinking himself blind in Tâkhdar at Kheb Hanût. You have found Hanâth's husband in the cellars. You should greet him and see if he is sober enough to ascend.\n",
[11242]="7002F995\n1\tDiscover the source of corruption\tDraugar have begun to spill from the mouth of a cave near the spot where the salamanders show signs of corruption.\n2\tDefeat draugar in Dwolung Hole (total: 12)\tDwolung Hole can be found in the bog west of Harwick where the salamanders grow corrupted. You should defeat the Draugar who begin to spill from the mouth of Dwolung Hole, spreading the pollution of death to the living.\n3\tReturn to Céolstan at the Harwick Stables\tCéolstan can be found within Harwick's stables. You should speak with Céolstan of the draugar in Dwolung Hole.\n",
[11243]="700595FC\n1\tPlay the Spring Seasonal Instances during the Spring Festival\tSpring Seasonal Instances have arrived! Play Spring Seasonal Instances during the Spring Festival. You can access Spring Seasonal Instances from the Instance Join panel.\n2\tPlay the Spring Seasonal Instances during the Spring Festival\tSpring Seasonal Instances have arrived! Play Spring Seasonal Instances during the Spring Festival. You can access Spring Seasonal Instances from the Instance Join panel.\n",
[11244]="7001A4AA\n1\tFind an Orc-trap\tOrc-traps might be found anywhere between Echad Glamodúd and Ashúrz Maufulug, to the south and a little west. Glamodúd has asked you to find and disarm any traps the Orcs may have placed in the Mirk-eaves.\n2\tDisarm Orc-traps (total: 10)\tOrc-traps might be found anywhere between Echad Glamodúd and Ashúrz Maufulug, to the south-west. Glamodúd has asked you to find and disarm any traps the Orcs may have placed in the Mirk-eaves. Now that you have seen one of the Orc-traps, the rest should be much easier to find.\n3\tTalk to Glamodúd at Echad Glamodúd\tGlamodúd is at Echad Glamodúd, north-east of Ashúrz Maufulug. You have disarmed many of the Orcs' traps and should now return to Glamodúd with your report.\n",
[11245]="700561DF\n1\tPull up weeds (total: 6)\tWeeds can be found in the Rohan Eastfold Homesteads. You should pull up weeds.\n",
[11246]="70003808\n1\tBring the mortar ingredients to Tindr\030Collect gypsum (total: 5)\030Collect sand (total: 5)\030Collect stones (total: 5)\tTindr is in the courtyard in front of Thorin's Hall. Sand is in the Rockbelly Pit south-east of Frerin's Court in a place called Winterheight. Gypsum and small stones can be found in the Mirkstone Tunnels above Frerin's Court to the north-west. Tindr, the Master Builder of Thorin's Hall, has asked you to collect various ingredients for a mortar with which to repair a leak in the canal wall.\n",
[11247]="7004429B\n1\tDefeat enemies upon the Hillock (total: 10)\tThe Hillock can be found in Pelennor Fields, north-east of the South-gate. You should defeat enemies upon the Hillock.\n2\tSpeak with Turgon\tTurgon can be found at the South-gate of the Rammas. You should speak with Turgon.\n",
[11248]="700017AD\n1\tScout the goblin camp\tThe goblins have established a camp on the southern hills of Annúndir, east of Amon Raith. Amarion has asked you to scout the goblin camp and assess the threat it poses to those under his care. He has warned you to take care. If a goblin sees you, it might track you back to Amon Raith. NOTE: Take care to remain unnoticed by the enemy. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tApproach the distraught man\tThe man in need of aid can be found just outside of the goblin stronghold in the central North Downs. You should speak with the man.\n",
[11249]="70062AA3\n1\tTalk to Skardí Bendblade in his blacksmith shop\tSkardí Bendblade is inside the blacksmith shop in the centre of town.\n2\tApply some grease to the hinges of Skardí's interior door and end the squeaking\tThe hinges of Skardí's interior door has developed a bit of a squeak.\n3\tApply some grease to the hinges of the healer's shop door and end the squeaking\tThe door to the healer's shop in the town square is in need of oiling.\n4\tThe squeaky hinges of the door to Cadogan's house are located west of the town square in Mossward.\t\n5\tTalk to Merion at the east gate of Mossward\tMerion of the town guard stands at the east gate of Mossward, waiting to hear of your success against the squeaky doors of the village.\n",
[11250]="7000D1CA\n1\tPick up a sack of grain\tThe sack of grain is near the silo on Hengstacer's Farm, east of Gaelm. Gaelm has instructed you to pick up a sack of grain near the silo at Hengstacer Farm and bring it to Bill Rosewood, the Stable-master near the West-gate of Bree.\n2\tTalk to Bill Rosewood\tBill Rosewood is at the stables near the West-gate of Bree, to the south of the Hengstacer Farm. You should speak with Bill Rosewood at his stable.\n3\tDraw water from the Boar Fountain\tThe Boar Fountain is south of The Prancing Pony Inn in Bree. Bill Rosewood has asked you to draw water from the Boar Fountain in Bree and use it to muck out one of his stalls by the West-gate of Bree.\n4\tTalk to Bill Rosewood\tBill Rosewood is at the stable near the South-gate of Bree. You mucked out one of Bill Rosewood's stalls, but he mentioned that Bert Goldenleaf, who maintains the stalls by the South-gate of Bree, may need the same service. You should speak with Bill Rosewood again before you leave.\n5\tDraw water from the Boar Fountain\tThe Boar Fountain is south of The Prancing Pony Inn in Bree. Bert Goldenleaf is at the stable near Bree's South-gate. Bill Rosewood told you to draw some water from the Boar Fountain in Bree and use it to muck out one of Bert Goldenleaf's stalls.\n6\tTalk to Bert Goldenleaf\tBert Goldenleaf is at his stable near the South-gate of Bree. You should speak with Bert Goldenleaf to see if there is anything else he would ask of you.\n7\tTalk to Gaelm\tReturn to Gaelm at the Hengstacer Farm in the Bree-fields, north of Bree. You have done all that the Stable-masters of Bree have asked of you. Now you can return to Gaelm and see if he will allow you to ride one of his tame mounts.\n",
[11251]="7000D1CB\n1\tPick up a sack of grain\tPick up a sack of grain near the silo east of Gaelm at Hengstacer Farm. Once you have it, bring it to Bill Rosewood, the Stable-master who is found near the West-gate of Bree.\n2\tTalk to Bill Rosewood\tSpeak to Bill Rosewood at his stables near the West-gate of Bree.\n3\tDraw water from the Bree boar fountain\tBill Rosewood has asked you to draw water from the Boar Fountain in Bree and use it to muck out one of his stalls by the West Gate of Bree.\n4\tTalk to Bill Rosewood\tSpeak to Bill Rosewood at the stables by the West Gate in Bree. You mucked out one of Bill Rosewood's stalls, but he mentioned that Bert Goldenleaf, who maintains the stalls by the South Gate of Bree, may need the same service.\n5\tDraw water from the Bree boar fountain\tDraw some water from the Boar Fountain in Bree and use it to muck out one of Bert Goldenleaf's stalls. Bert Goldenleaf's stables can be found by the South Gate of Bree.\n6\tTalk to Bert Goldenleaf\tSpeak to Bert Goldenleaf to see if there is anything else he would ask of you. You also mucked out one of Bert Goldenleaf's stalls, as you did for Bill Rosewood.\n7\tTalk to Gaelm\tReturn to Gaelm at Hengstacer Farm in the Bree-fields. You have done all that the Stable-masters of Bree have asked of you, so now you can return to Gaelm and see if he will now allow you to ride one of his tame mounts.\n",
[11252]="700700AF\n1\tComplete Quest: Shooing Shrews\030Complete Quest: Saving the Apples\030Complete Quest: Rescuing the Vegetables\030Complete Quest: Lost Hobbits\030Complete Quest: Vanished Valuables\030Complete Quest: Kick Out the Cave-claws\tConstable Tanglerush suggests talking to some of the hobbits around Staddle and seeing if there is anything you can do to help them with their current woes.\n2\tTalk to Constable Tanglerush in Staddle\tYou have done what you can to help the hobbits of Staddle. You should return to Constable Tanglerush for the reward she promised.\n",
[11253]="700700B2\n1\tTalk to Constable Tanglerush in Staddle\tHumbert claims that Staddle is under attack and has asked you to go there and help the village. You should go there and ask one of the constables what is going on. Staddle is in Bree-land, just south-east of Bree-town.\n",
[11254]="7003A5D9\n1\tTalk to Cúthing\tCúthing is standing near Meregyth, outside the Mead Hall of Beaconwatch. Meregyth asked you to speak with Cúthing and learn what he has planned.\n2\tCollapse White Mountain cave-entrances (total: 2)\tThe cave-entrances lie to the west of Beaconwatch. Cúthing asked you to collapse the entrances of the Orcs' caves.\n3\tTalk to Cúthing\tCúthing is standing near Meregyth, outside the Mead Hall of Beaconwatch. You should return to Beaconwatch and let Cúthing know about your success.\n",
[11255]="70036DC8\n1\tDefeat waves of enemies ([see journal]/6)\tProtect the barricades at the end of the island bridge and stop the enemy from damaging Gamling's ballista.\n",
[11256]="700380E9\n1\tDefeat waves of enemies ([see journal]/6)\030Defeat the trolls\tProtect the barricades at the end of the island bridge and stop the enemy from damaging Gamling's ballista.\n",
[11257]="7001A640\n1\tDefeat swamp-cats in the Drownholt (total: 10)\tSwamp-cats can be found in the drowned lands of the Drownholt, all around Estolad Mernael. Laidhriel has asked you to defeat many of the hunting swamp-cats that stalk the camp.\n2\tTalk to Laidhriel at Estolad Mernael\tLaidhriel can be found at Estolad Mernael, the Malledhrim camp in the Drownholt. You should speak with Laidhriel and tell her of your success against the evil swamp-cats of the drowned lands.\n",
[11258]="70054678\n1\tCheck this stage in the quest journal.\t\n2\tDefeat Stalker Thimmoth\tStalker Thimmoth can be found scouting the Circle of Madness. You should defeat Stalker Thimmoth\n3\tCompleted\t\n",
[11259]="7001BA43\n1\tHaudh Methernil, the Barrow of Ringdor, and the Barrow of Taradan are scattered across the northern Barrow-downs. Broderic Willowmeade has asked you to travel deep within Haudh Methernil, the Barrow of Ringdor, and the Barrow of Taradan and defeat either Gwinon the spider, Marrow the kergrim, or Umnen the darkwater.\t\n2\tTalk to Broderic Willowmeade in Bree\tBroderic Willowmeade can be found near the Hunting Lodge in the Haunted Alley in Bree. You should return to Broderic Willowmeade with news of your success.\n",
[11260]="70047D67\n1\tFind Warg tracks (total: 8)\tWarg tracks can be found near the Camp of the Host. Follow the trail to find The Stalker.\n2\tDefeat Múgbakh, The Stalker\tFind and defeat Múgbakh, the Stalker, with the help of Faroth. Faroth must be present to find Múgbakh. If you lose track of him, use the hound-calling whistle to summon him back.\n3\tReturn to Mablung\tMablung can be found at the Camp of the Host. You should return to Mablung and tell him you have defeated Múgbakh, The Stalker.\n",
[11261]="700173C9\n1\tDefeat Highpeak-trainers (total: 3)\030Defeat Highpeak-stalkers (total: 6)\tThe Warg-rider scouts and trainers can be found within the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch. Thithrand fears that the forces of the Warg-riders will grow into a fearsome unit if they are are not stopped from completing their goals.\n2\tTalk to Thithrand at the Orc-watch\tThithrand is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair. You should return to Thithrand at the Orc-watch and tell him that you have defeated the goblins.\n",
[11262]="7006658E\n1\tDefeat Burnalg within Gaerlond\tCúdor has asked you to travel to Gaerlond and find the Orc's armour. Once there, ring the bell he gave you and defeat the Orc. Gaerlond is north-east of Barad Rill.\n2\tTalk to Cúdor in Barad Rill\tCúdor will be thrilled to hear that the threat of the Orcs has stopped here. Cúdor can be found in Barad Rill.\n",
[11263]="70028AD0\n1\tAssist Fraid with thieves at the Galtrev Lumber-camp\030Assist Fraid with stolen stacks of lumber\tThe driver of the wood-waggon has become lost somewhere between Galtrev and the nearby Galtrev Lumber-camp to the north. You should search for the missing driver and help the missing shipment reach Galtrev.\n2\tTalk to Fraid at his waggon\tFraid lies injured by his broken waggon in Pren Gwydh, near the Galtrev Lumber-camp. You should speak with Fraid again, now that you have helped to allay the threat of the Dragon-clan at the Galtrev Lumber-camp.\n",
[11264]="7000D4F1\n1\tDefeat Gorthorog Flayer (total: 10)\tThe gorthorog-flayers reside in and around the Bails of Himbar. Maerchiniath has instructed you to thin the numbers of the gorthorog-flayers.\n2\tTalk to Maerchiniath\tGath Forthnír is west of Himbar in the mountains. Having defeated many gertheryg, you should return to Maerchiniath and tell him of your success.\n",
})
